**Findings**
::code-comment{title="[P2] Existing v2 checkpoints can skip compact transcript backfill" body="This path now treats an existing v2 checkpoint as fully migrated whenever all `/full/*` raw artifacts are present. It no longer checks `existing.Sessions[i].Transcript`, so older/partial v2 checkpoints that have raw `/full` data but no `/main/transcript.jsonl` are skipped forever unless the user reruns with `--force`. The removed `backfillCompactTranscripts` test covered this exact compatibility case." file="/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go" start=323 end=339 priority=2 confidence=0.88}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Metadata-only read bypasses blob fetch fallback" body="`ReadSessionMetadata` reads `metadata.json` directly from the go-git tree. The v2 read paths normally use `wrapWithFetcher`, which also handles partial-clone/stale-packfile cases through `git cat-file` and the configured blob fetcher. Since migration reruns now call this helper in the partial-state hot path, repos where metadata blobs are fetchable but not visible to go-git can fail while the previous `ReadSessionMetadataAndPrompts` path would have recovered." file="/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_read.go" start=220 end=226 priority=2 confidence=0.76}

Reviewed `origin/main...origin/more-migration-speedups` from the GitHub compare. I also ran:

`go test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(Migrate|V2GitStore_BuildFullSessionArtifactsIndex|RepairV2GenerationMetadata)'`

That targeted suite passed, and `git diff --check` was clean.

